WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:03.560
OK, let's talk about Joe Biden on immigration
now.

00:00:03.560 --> 00:00:09.519
Joe Biden has made it clear that the immediate
next priority is covid relief.

00:00:09.519 --> 00:00:12.710
I've already criticized and said it should
have been done already.

00:00:12.710 --> 00:00:13.710
It hasn't.

00:00:13.710 --> 00:00:15.610
We're hoping that it gets done soon.

00:00:15.610 --> 00:00:17.460
Very soon thereafter.

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:19.769
Immigration is going to be high on Joe Biden's
list.

00:00:19.769 --> 00:00:25.369
Now, much of what Joe Biden wants to do on
immigration cannot be done by executive order.

00:00:25.369 --> 00:00:31.429
One bit of good news is that Joe Biden has
canceled the national emergency order that

00:00:31.429 --> 00:00:37.410
Donald Trump was using to try to get money
for his border wall.

00:00:37.410 --> 00:00:43.280
Joe Biden sent a letter to Congress late last
week saying that no further tax dollars will

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:44.780
be spent on the wall.

00:00:44.780 --> 00:00:48.180
Now, you might be wondering, but there was
no wall.

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:50.530
Trump promised a wall across the entire border.

00:00:50.530 --> 00:00:51.530
It never happened.

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:53.000
What are we talking about here?

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:54.550
That is true.

00:00:54.550 --> 00:00:58.460
But remember that Donald Trump declared a
state of emergency over the southern border

00:00:58.460 --> 00:01:04.980
in twenty nineteen that allowed him to use
some military funding for construction of

00:01:04.980 --> 00:01:05.980
the wall.

00:01:05.980 --> 00:01:11.650
Now, the disastrous news is that Trump did
manage to spend twenty five billion on the

00:01:11.650 --> 00:01:12.850
project.

00:01:12.850 --> 00:01:17.190
The unfortunate it's sort of like a Pyrrhic
victory that Donald Trump had because he was

00:01:17.190 --> 00:01:21.410
able to obtain money for the wall, but they
were really able to do mostly some replacement

00:01:21.410 --> 00:01:26.180
of existing border wall areas with a new type
of wall and expand it slightly.

00:01:26.180 --> 00:01:31.659
So as far as a campaign promise, Trump failed
on having a wall across the entire border.

00:01:31.659 --> 00:01:32.659
That was his promise.

00:01:32.659 --> 00:01:36.880
He made it very, very clearly and said that
was a first term accomplishment that he would

00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:37.880
have.

00:01:37.880 --> 00:01:38.880
Didn't happen.

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:45.030
On the other hand, it's it's good news in
the sense that not much of it took place.

00:01:45.030 --> 00:01:52.140
And Joe Biden is able to shut down this emergency
declaration of emergency and to stop pulling

00:01:52.140 --> 00:01:55.680
any more money from the military for the wall.

00:01:55.680 --> 00:02:01.160
This is the continued use of executive orders
by Joe Biden to undo many of the disasters

00:02:01.160 --> 00:02:02.290
that Donald Trump did.

00:02:02.290 --> 00:02:07.500
Of course, much like debt and deficit, executive
orders have become a political football.

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:13.240
If your guy or gal is in power and using executive
orders, then you say these executive orders

00:02:13.240 --> 00:02:18.090
are required and necessary to undo the damage
of the previous president.

00:02:18.090 --> 00:02:24.340
If your guy or gal is not in the Oval Office,
then you call executive orders, at least if

00:02:24.340 --> 00:02:33.270
you're a Republican, a sort of authoritarian,
tyrannical circumvention of the normal legislative

00:02:33.270 --> 00:02:34.270
process.

00:02:34.270 --> 00:02:35.569
That's that's the way it's been for a while.

00:02:35.569 --> 00:02:38.850
It's pretty similar to the debt and deficit.

00:02:38.850 --> 00:02:43.870
But it is a good thing that Joe Biden has
been doing this, particularly when the Republican

00:02:43.870 --> 00:02:48.650
Party is more obstructionist, arguably, than
it has ever been.

00:02:48.650 --> 00:02:53.600
The exact numbers are that 80 miles of new
barriers were built during the Trump administration

00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:55.090
where there were none.

00:02:55.090 --> 00:02:59.900
And otherwise there were just replacements
of existing parts of border wall or border

00:02:59.900 --> 00:03:00.900
fencing.

00:03:00.900 --> 00:03:07.209
So I think this is an important time to just
remind you that we know a lot about what circumstances

00:03:07.209 --> 00:03:11.330
call for a wall and what circumstances do
not.

00:03:11.330 --> 00:03:16.069
One of the really interesting things is that
even without the wall, remember Trump only.

00:03:16.069 --> 00:03:23.380
Added 80 miles without a wall across the entire
border, as promised by Trump.

00:03:23.380 --> 00:03:27.760
Trump regularly claimed border crossings are
lower than ever.

00:03:27.760 --> 00:03:35.450
So that's proof that if you believe that,
that's proof that it is not a wall that reduces

00:03:35.450 --> 00:03:36.510
border crossings.

00:03:36.510 --> 00:03:42.310
And of course, we've long studied the reasons
why it is absurd to spend these ungodly amounts

00:03:42.310 --> 00:03:43.620
of money on a wall.

00:03:43.620 --> 00:03:44.620
We know that.

00:03:44.620 --> 00:03:50.270
And we've seen examples of being able to scale
the wall with about one hundred dollars in

00:03:50.270 --> 00:03:55.140
parts from any hardware store, Home Depot,
Lowe's, that type of place.

00:03:55.140 --> 00:03:56.629
It is easily defeated.

00:03:56.629 --> 00:04:02.540
Number two, you have a significant portion
of people who are in the United States illegally

00:04:02.540 --> 00:04:07.150
who have overstayed visas or came for tourism
and never left.

00:04:07.150 --> 00:04:13.930
And they are mostly flying in, not crossing
the physical border at the US Mexico border.

00:04:13.930 --> 00:04:19.900
And then lastly, if you want to think about
the best ROIC y the best return on investment

00:04:19.900 --> 00:04:24.779
for dealing with the issue of undocumented
immigration, we really should be approaching

00:04:24.779 --> 00:04:30.819
this from why are people wanting to come to
the United States to begin with understanding

00:04:30.819 --> 00:04:37.589
the economic conditions in the source countries,
not just Mexico, but further south as well,

00:04:37.589 --> 00:04:39.599
and working with those countries?

00:04:39.599 --> 00:04:46.059
And if we are supposed to be sort of agnostic
to how the money is spent, as long as it effectively

00:04:46.059 --> 00:04:50.699
deals with the undocumented immigration problem,
then you would think that the right would

00:04:50.699 --> 00:04:56.490
be open to the ideas of economists and others
who have said, well, let's instead of building

00:04:56.490 --> 00:05:00.830
a wall that can be defeated and won't actually
address a lot of the people that fly in and

00:05:00.830 --> 00:05:06.370
overstay visas or just never leave when they
come over for vacation, let's actually spend

00:05:06.370 --> 00:05:10.020
money by improving economic circumstances
in some of these source countries.

00:05:10.020 --> 00:05:13.919
Now, the problem is we know that for them.

00:05:13.919 --> 00:05:19.919
A big aspect of this is not just doing what's
most effective, it's what doing what feels

00:05:19.919 --> 00:05:25.860
right based on their framework of morality,
as they would call it, or maybe as we would

00:05:25.860 --> 00:05:27.520
describe it.

00:05:27.520 --> 00:05:35.879
And to them, it would seem wrong in some way
to give money to improve a country when people

00:05:35.879 --> 00:05:37.430
are coming here illegally.

00:05:37.430 --> 00:05:43.080
It just doesn't feel right to the ideology
that many of these right wingers are committed

00:05:43.080 --> 00:05:44.080
to.

00:05:44.080 --> 00:05:48.029
But study after study, as we've outlined in
our long form piece about this issue, confirms

00:05:48.029 --> 00:05:52.270
that that actually would be the most effective
way to curb undocumented immigration to the

00:05:52.270 --> 00:05:53.270
United States.

00:05:53.270 --> 00:05:57.999
So the micro story, Joe Biden has cut that
emergency declaration.

00:05:57.999 --> 00:06:02.189
There is not even a mechanism with which you
could pull money from the military to build

00:06:02.189 --> 00:06:03.629
the wall.

00:06:03.629 --> 00:06:06.289
Next step as Biden's got to deal with DACA.

00:06:06.289 --> 00:06:10.569
And it is finally time with Democrats controlling
the White House, the House and the Senate.

00:06:10.569 --> 00:06:14.180
If it's not going to happen now, I don't know
that it will ever happen.

00:06:14.180 --> 00:06:18.999
It's finally time to really do the immigration
reform we've been talking about for I mean,

00:06:18.999 --> 00:06:21.550
it's been 15 years or longer at this point.

00:06:21.550 --> 00:06:22.550
Send me your thoughts.

00:06:22.550 --> 00:06:47.559
You can find me on Twitter at 

00:06:47.559 --> 00:07:21.669
David Pakman, T

